# Talk locale Korean (noun-first keywords)

When adding or editing `assets/locale/talk/<city>.json` (or any town dialogue KO overlay):

## Topics and aliases

- `topic1` / `topic2` must be **short Korean nouns** that appear in the spoken lines
  (interest highlight / discovery / the keyword-row label).
- `topicN_aliases` keep **Latin classic stems** (`food`, `rune`, `writ`, `smok`…).
  Extra Korean type-in synonyms are allowed when players would type a close form
  (`없다` for `없음`); those match keyboard input only and must **not** be the
  primary label — they are not tinted and must not appear on the keyword row.
- Do **not** add extra Korean synonyms that never appear in dialogue just to
  guess what a player might invent.
- Do **not** use:
  - verb stems (`먹`, `도와`, `돌보`, `죽`, `부르`, `듣`)
  - conjugations (`먹었어`, `도와주세요`)
  - particles on the keyword itself (`룬을`, `무기를`)
  - adjective-only forms as the primary label when a noun exists (`가난한` → prefer `가난`)
- Short verb stems prefix-match every conjugation (`먹` → `먹었/먹었어/…`); avoid them unless intentionally wanted.

## Dialogue lines (`job`, `response*`, etc.)

- Natural Korean is fine; particles and verbs in **running text** are OK.
- Prefer wording that includes the **topic noun** so interest highlight and player cues line up
  (e.g. `음식이 필요해요` not only `배가 고파요` when the topic is `음식` / `배고픔`).
- Builtin interests stay noun-ish too: `직업`, `건강`, `이름`, `모습`, `주기`, `합류`, `관심사`.

## LOOK + meet/see (required check)

Engine builds: `당신은 {명사}을/를 만났다/보았다.` from `ko.look` via `TalkLocale._look_ko_to_noun`.

- Write LOOK as a **predicate sentence** ending `다.` / `이다.` / `다!` (e.g. `키 큰 마법사다.`, `장난기 많은 아이다.`).
- After each city pack (or when changing look lines), verify meet for **every** NPC:
  - Copula strip must leave a **full noun**: `아이` not `아`, `대장장이` not `대장장`, `여인` not `여인이`.
  - Nouns that end in **이** + `다` (아이, ~장이) are especially easy to mangle if stripped as `이다`.
  - Result particle must fit (받침 → 을, else 를).
- If a new stem ends in open-syllable **이** and is not already handled (`아이`, `장이` in `_look_stem_ends_with_open_i_noun`), extend that list or rephrase the look (e.g. prefer `…이다` after batchim stems).
- Never write LOOK so that “You meet” reads as **“당신은 …이다”** identity (“you are …”).

## Reference

- Pack format: `TalkLocale` + `assets/locale/talk/minoc.json`
- Matching: prefix on normalized Hangul; highlight tints **keyword only** (조사 제외)
- Meet/see conversion: `src/core/talk_locale.gd` (`_you_encounter_ko`, `_look_ko_to_noun`)
